u, Doorwerth Castle","dish/beaulieu-doorwerth-castle"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Bell's (restaurant)","dish/bell-s-restaurant"],["Belmond Le Manoir aux Quat'Saisons","dish/belmond-le-manoir-aux-quat-saisons"],["Beluga (restaurant)","dish/beluga-restaurant"],["Berowra Waters Inn","dish/berowra-waters-inn"],["Beurre maître d'hôtel","dish/beurre-maitre-d-hotel"],["Beurre manié","dish/beurre-manie"],["Bisque (food)","dish/bisque-food"],["Bistro 990","dish/bistro-990"],["Bistro Agnes","dish/bistro-agnes"],["Bistro Jeanty","dish/bistro-jeanty"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/fa/Narisawa_restaurant.jpg/500px-Narisawa_restaurant.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Pocsywe","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Narisawa_restaurant.jpg"}},"dish/popoca":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/popoca","n":"Popoca","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Salvadoran cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Popoca is a restaurant in Oakland, California, United States. Anthony Salguero is the chef. The restaurant serves Salvadoran cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-popoca"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popoca"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Salvadoran cuisine","cuisine/salvadoran-cuisine"]]}]},"ingredient/milk-skin":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/milk-skin","n":"Milk skin","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Milk skin or lactoderm is a sticky film of protein that forms on top of dairy milk and foods containing dairy milk (such as hot chocolate and some soups). Milk skin, or the lactoderm can be produced both through conventional boiling and by microwaving the liquid, and as such can often be observed when heating milk for use in drinks such as drinking chocolate. It is caused by the denaturation of proteins such as beta-lactoglobulin (whey protein). The strong thickness of the skin varies dependent on a number of factors, including the temperature of the milk, the shape of the container, and the amount of milk in the container."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-milk-skin"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milk_skin"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Bengali cuisine","cuisine/bengali-cuisine",[["Sarbhaja","dish/sarbhaja"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Ghee","ingredient/ghee"],["Kheer (Bengali sweets)","ingredient/kheer-bengali-sweets"],["Maida (flour)","ingredient/maida-flour"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/85/Double_skin_milk.jpg/500px-Double_skin_milk.jpg","w":500,"h":576,"by":"Guanlin (Gary) He","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Double_skin_milk.jpg"}},"dish/sate-taichan":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sate-taichan","n":"Sate taichan","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Sate taichan is a variation of chicken satay grilled and served without peanut or kecap seasoning unlike other satays. It is served with sambal and squeezed key lime, while the chicken meat used with this satay is generally plain white in colour and only seasoned with salt, key lime, and chili. Like other satays, sate taichan is sold at night."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sate-taichan"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sate_taichan"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Lime","ingredient/lime"],["Peanut","ingredient/peanut"],["Sambal","ingredient/sambal"],["Shallot","ing